            "review_title": "Review at Cơm Gà Sài Gòn V.Hải",
            "review_text": "Tung T\n6 contributions\n0\nGood & inexpensive Vietnamese restaurant near Châu Thị Vĩnh Tế Street in Danang\nMar 2024 • Solo\nI highly recommend the restaurant Bún Bò Huế V.Hải if you are looking for a good and inexpensive Vietnamese restaurant near the area of Châu Thị Vĩnh Tế Street in Danang. As of today, March 12, 2024, I have been frequenting this restaurant every night since February 18, 2024. I have been going there on a daily basis because I like its variety of freshly made food, good service, and reasonable prices. When I dine in, usually during the hours of 8:30 – 10:00 PM, the restaurant is not crowded, and the customers are not loud. I typically order their most expensive dine-in meal selections, which have plenty of freshly cooked meat but are only 60K VND. After eating there, I also take out daily at least three of its 15K–25K VND medium-sized Bánh Mìs that are all oven-toasted hot, have plenty of meat, and are very flavourful. These are the best-tasting Bánh Mìs for less than 30,000 VND that I have ever eaten in my life. By the way, I’m 60 years old, of Vietnamese descent, get no compensation whatsoever, and have no relationship with any person who is associated with the restaurant Bún Bò Huế V.Hải.\nRead more\nInsider tip:\nI recommend very good value 15K-25K VND Bánh Mìs because they are medium size, oven-toasted hot, have plenty of meat, & are very flavourful.\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nWritten March 12, 2024",
